<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Research impact principles">
  <div><strong>Impact has stages</strong><span>Mechanism, product evidence, adoption and outcomes are different milestones.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Context matters</strong><span>Results from one population or setting do not automatically transfer to another.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Implementation counts</strong><span>A useful idea still has to be accessible, practical and sustainable in the real world.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">From evidence to impact</p>
    <h2>Do not skip the middle</h2>
    <p>Established physiology can guide formulation and study design. Product claims need product-specific evidence. Real-world impact then depends on whether people can access, prepare and use the solution as intended.</p>
    <p>Those stages can inform one another, but they are not interchangeable.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Impact pathway</p>
  <h2>Five useful stages</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__steps">
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Understand the mechanism</h3><p>Clarify the relevant physiology and its limits.</p></article>
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Build the product</h3><p>Define the formulation, preparation and intended use.</p></article>
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Test the actual product</h3><p>Study the formulation under conditions that match the claim of interest.</p></article>
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Test real-world use</h3><p>Measure access, preparation, tolerance, adoption and delivery.</p></article>
    <article class="bhd-page__step"><h3>Measure outcomes</h3><p>Only then describe measured health, performance, access or cost outcomes as impact.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Different settings, different evidence</p>
  <h2>What impact can mean</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3">
    <article><h3>Performance</h3><p>Practical hydration use, tolerance and relevant athlete outcomes under the conditions being studied.</p><a href="/pages/performance-hydration">Performance Hydration →</a></article>
    <article><h3>Clinical</h3><p>Evidence in the relevant patient population, with appropriate endpoints, governance and care integration.</p><a href="/pages/clinical-development">Clinical Development →</a></article>
    <article><h3>Humanitarian</h3><p>Preparation reliability, access, affordability, water safety, local fit and appropriate formulation.</p><a href="/pages/eco-humanitarian">Humanitarian Hydration →</a></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">What we measure</p>
    <h2>Activity is not the same as outcome</h2>
    <p>Useful implementation measures can include reach, acceptability, feasibility, adoption, fidelity, cost and sustainability. Hydration projects may also track preparation accuracy, adherence, tolerance and distribution reliability.</p>
    <p>Samples distributed, meetings held or partnerships announced describe activity. They do not by themselves show better hydration, health or performance.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Impact rule</span>
    <h3>Claim the stage actually reached.</h3>
    <p>Say whether something is a rationale, study objective, measured finding or demonstrated outcome.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Humanitarian boundary</p>
    <h2>Consumer hydration and therapeutic ORS are not interchangeable</h2>
    <p>World Health Organization reduced-osmolarity oral rehydration salts are a defined therapeutic formulation for diarrhoeal dehydration. Humanitarian work must be clear about formulation, intended use, preparation and referral pathways.</p>
  </div>
</section>

